          "name": "Add State Qualifiers for Named Cities in Event Memories",
          "description": "When extracting or updating an event memory that names a specific city or place, add its commonly known state or country qualifier.",
          "content": [
            "During extraction or update of an event memory, if the message names a specific city or place (e.g., Tampa), add a concise qualifier for its well-known larger region (e.g., Florida).",
            "Use only obvious common knowledge; do not research, speculate, or add unmentioned details beyond the commonly known region.",
            "Preserve the original named place and activity; the qualifier is supplementary so future questions about state or country can be answered.",
            "Stop after adding the known region; do not list multiple possible locations or expand the memory further."
          ]
        },
        "solves": "Construction sometimes stores event memories with a named city but omits the well-known state or country, so later questions about the larger region cannot be answered from the memory. This skill ensures event memories include obvious geographic qualifiers for named places.",
